               <msContents>
                  <summary/>
                  <msItem xml:id="ms_i0">
                     <locus from="1v" to="14v">1v-14v</locus>
                     <textLang xml:lang="ar">Arabic</textLang>
                     <title ref="LIT0049IHA#s33IHA"/>
                     <incipit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#1v">-1v</locus>ِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَنِ الرَّحِيْمِ حم تَنْزِيْلُ الكِتَابِ مِنَ اللهِ العَزِيْزِ الحَكِيْمِ</incipit>
                     <explicit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#14v">-14v</locus>قَالُوْا كَذَلِكَ قَالَ رَبُّكِ إِنَّهُ هُّوَ الحَكِيمُ العَليْمُ</explicit>
                     <note>46:1-51:30. Fourteen, sometime fifteen lines a page. Titles of sūras rubricated. Very few words left uncompleted at the end of a line, rewritten in full on the following line. Diacritics and vowels were written using a thinner qalam. Catchwords. In the margins, mark of ḥizb in red color (8v), and of ǧuz’ (1v, together with two 5 pointed stars), few corrections by another hand. The identification of the scribe is based on notes in ASH00276 (fol. 13r) and ASH00265 (fol. 1r).</note>
                     <note/>
                  </msItem>
